Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dp: Handle a PLL unlock interrupt while AUX is idle

Reinitializing the DP PHY during a modeset can raise PLL_UNLOCKED while
no AUX transfer is pending. The controller already acknowledged the
interrupt before dispatching it. Return IRQ_HANDLED for this standalone
status without logging an AUX error or signaling transfer completion.
Keep the existing handling for all other statuses.

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_aux.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_aux.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_aux.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_aux.c
@@ -465,6 +465,10 @@ irqreturn_t msm_dp_aux_isr(struct drm_dp_aux *msm_dp_aux, u32 isr)
 	aux = container_of(msm_dp_aux, struct msm_dp_aux_private, msm_dp_aux);
 
 	if (!aux->cmd_busy) {
+		/* The controller already acknowledged the PHY's PLL status. */
+		if (isr == DP_INTR_PLL_UNLOCKED)
+			return IRQ_HANDLED;
+
 		DRM_ERROR("Unexpected DP AUX IRQ %#010x when not busy\n", isr);
 		return IRQ_NONE;
 	}
